IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fbtaa-employee`

-- Fringe Benefits Tax Assessment Act 1986 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- amounts the employee baseline could not compute,
-- now computed from the formulas the Federal Register prints as images: the reportable fringe benefits amount of an employee
-- of a charity, hospital, ambulance service or other s 57A or s 58 employer (s 135Q(2) to (4)), which `My reportable fringe
-- benefits amount` answers `not covered`; and the taxable value of a car under the cost basis (s 10(2), (3), (5)), with the
-- deemed depreciation and interest of an owned car (s 11(1A), (1), (1AA), (1B), (2)), its depreciated value (s 12(1)) and the
-- business use percentage (s 136(1)).
--
-- A module beside fbtaa-employee.l4 and fbtaa-seat-employer.l4 (24 October 2026). They stay as they are; this module calls
-- their rules (`the rate of fringe benefits tax for`, `My reportable fringe benefits amount`, `The taxable value of my car`,
-- `the number of days in the year of tax`) rather than restating them. Its employee questions come first; the employer's
-- mirror questions follow under their own heading, with their own names.
--
-- SEAT: the employee receiving a benefit ("What is my reportable fringe benefits amount?", "What is the taxable value of my
-- car if my employer uses the cost basis?"); and, mirrored, the employer.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 97 (register id C2026C00332), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03280.txt. The
-- formulas are images the text deposit dropped; they are transcribed in ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03280.formulas.md
-- (entries s 135Q(4), s 10(2), s 11(1A), (1), (1AA), (1B), (2), s 12(1), s 136(1)(d); recovered 2026-10-24).
--
-- INPUTS THAT ARE NOT LAW. The statutory interest rate (s 136(1): the RBA's benchmark rate, REQ-0110, not deposited); the
-- diminishing value percentage of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 (s 11(1AA): "the percentage applicable in using the
-- diminishing value method (within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997) as at the start of the year of tax" --
-- 200% under that Act's s 40-72(1) for a car held from 10 May 2006, asked here because it is another Act's figure); the
-- Commissioner's effective life determination (s 11(1AA), ITAA 1997 s 40-100); the car expenses and the lease charges.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. A car held by the provider for only part of its ownership in the year (s 11(1A), (1B) are encoded, but the seat
-- question takes the holding period to be the whole of the days owned in the year, so their fraction is 1); a car neither owned
-- nor leased (s 10(3)(a)(vi)); non-business accessories under the cost basis (s 10(3)(a)(iv)); a car owned on 1 July 1986
-- (s 12(2)); the change of identity rules (s 10(3B)-(3D)); log book periods and records (ss 10A, 10B, 162B to 162K: whether the
-- employer may reduce the operating cost is one fact); s 13 (non-arm's length expenditure); the s 135Q exempt benefits
-- themselves (which benefits are exempt under ss 57A, 58 is asked as the quasi-fringe benefits amount).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Fringe Benefits Tax Assessment Act 1986 -- amounts from the formulas`

§§ `s 135Q -- my reportable fringe benefits amount from a s 57A or s 58 employer`

-- s 135Q(2): "The employee has a reportable fringe benefits amount (worked out under subsection (4)) for the year of income ...
-- if the sum of the following is more than $2,000: (a) the employee's individual fringe benefits amount (if any) ...; (b) the
-- employee's individual quasi-fringe benefits amount". (3): the quasi amount is what the individual fringe benefits amount would
-- be if each benefit exempt under s 57A or s 58 (or s 8A) "were a fringe benefit" and there were no other fringe benefits.
-- (4), from the authorised rendering:
--     (Individual fringe benefits amount + Individual quasi-fringe benefits amount) × (1 / (1 − Rate of tax))
-- (5): "This section has effect despite section 135P."
@export What is my reportable fringe benefits amount from a charity, hospital, ambulance service or other s 57A or s 58 employer (s 135Q)?
GIVEN `my individual fringe benefits amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable value of the fringe benefits this employer provided to you in the FBT year that are not exempt (often nil for a s 57A employer)
      `my individual quasi-fringe benefits amount` IS A NUMBER @desc What that amount would be if the benefits exempt under s 57A or s 58 (or s 8A) were fringe benefits and there were no others: their total taxable value, leaving out excluded fringe benefits
      `the FBT year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which that FBT year started
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`My reportable fringe benefits amount from a s 57A or s 58 employer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the rate of fringe benefits tax for` `the FBT year starting in`
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN `not covered` r
    WHEN `answered` rate THEN
        IF `the sum` GREATER THAN 2000
        THEN `answered` (`the sum` TIMES (1 DIVIDED BY (1 MINUS rate)))
        ELSE `answered` 0
    WHERE
        `the sum` MEANS `my individual fringe benefits amount` PLUS `my individual quasi-fringe benefits amount`

-- The question for any employer: s 135Q for a s 57A or s 58 employer, otherwise fbtaa-employee.l4's s 135P answer.
@export What is my reportable fringe benefits amount for this employer, whatever kind of employer it is (ss 135P, 135Q)?
GIVEN `my individual fringe benefits amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The total taxable value of the non-exempt fringe benefits this employer provided to you in the FBT year, including an exempt electric car, leaving out excluded fringe benefits
      `my individual quasi-fringe benefits amount` IS A NUMBER @desc For a s 57A or s 58 employer, the total taxable value its exempt benefits to you would have if they were fringe benefits; 0 for any other employer
      `the FBT year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which that FBT year started
      `my employer is a charity, hospital, ambulance service or other s 57A or s 58 employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is a public benevolent institution, health promotion charity, public or non-profit hospital, public ambulance service, or an employer of the kind in s 58
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`My reportable fringe benefits amount, any employer` MEANS
    IF `my employer is a charity, hospital, ambulance service or other s 57A or s 58 employer`
    THEN `My reportable fringe benefits amount from a s 57A or s 58 employer` `my individual fringe benefits amount` `my individual quasi-fringe benefits amount` `the FBT year starting in`
    ELSE `My reportable fringe benefits amount` `my individual fringe benefits amount` `the FBT year starting in` FALSE

§§ `ss 11, 12 -- deemed depreciation and interest on an owned car`

-- s 11(1AA), from the authorised rendering:   DV percentage / Effective life of the car
GIVEN `DV percentage` IS A NUMBER, `effective life in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the depreciation rate B` MEANS
    `DV percentage` DIVIDED BY (100 TIMES `effective life in years`)

-- s 11(1):   ABC / D   -- "A is: (a) where the car was owned by the person at the beginning of the year of tax -- the depreciated
-- value of the car at that time; or (b) in any other case -- the cost price"; B from (1AA); "C is the number of days in the
-- period in the year of tax during which the car was owned by the person; and D is the number of days in the year of tax."
-- s 11(2): the same ABC / D for interest, with "B is the statutory interest rate in relation to the year of tax".
GIVEN `A` IS A NUMBER, `B` IS A NUMBER, `C` IS A NUMBER, `D` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 11 product` MEANS
    (`A` TIMES `B` TIMES `C`) DIVIDED BY `D`

-- s 11(1A):   DEP × (DHP / DCO)   and s 11(1B):   INT × (DHP / DCO) -- the share of the year's depreciation or interest for
-- the days of the holding period on which the person owned the car, over the days in the year it was owned.
GIVEN `year's amount` IS A NUMBER, `DHP` IS A NUMBER, `DCO` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the holding period share` MEANS
    (`year's amount` TIMES `DHP`) DIVIDED BY `DCO`

-- s 12(1):   A − B   -- "A is ... the cost price of the car to the person. B is the total amount of depreciation (if any) that
-- would have been taken to have been incurred by the person in respect of the car for the period after the start of 1 July 1986
-- and before the relevant time when the person owned the car, if ... calculated in accordance with subsection 11(1)."
-- Worked out year by year: in the year of tax the car was bought, s 11(1) on the cost price for the days owned; in each later
-- full year, on the depreciated value at its start for every day of the year (C = D, so B alone).
GIVEN `value` IS A NUMBER, `B` IS A NUMBER, `full years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`after full years` MEANS
    IF `full years` AT MOST 0 THEN `value`
    ELSE `after full years` (`value` MINUS `value` TIMES `B`) `B` (`full years` MINUS 1)

@export What is the depreciated value of my employer's car at the start of the FBT year (ss 11(1), 12(1))?
GIVEN `the car's cost price` IS A NUMBER @desc What the car cost your employer (or the provider) when it became the owner, in dollars
      `the FBT year it was bought in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the FBT year of the purchase started
      `days owned in that first FBT year` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from the purchase to 31 March at the end of that FBT year
      `the FBT year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the FBT year you are asking about starts (after the year of purchase)
      `DV percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 diminishing value percentage at the start of the year (200 for a car held from 10 May 2006, its s 40-72)
      `effective life in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The car's effective life in the Commissioner's determination under s 40-100 of the 1997 Act (8 years for most cars)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The depreciated value of the car at the start of the year` MEANS
    `after full years` `the value after the first year` `the rate` (`the FBT year starting in` MINUS `the FBT year it was bought in` MINUS 1)
    WHERE
        `the rate` MEANS `the depreciation rate B` `DV percentage` `effective life in years`
        `the first year's depreciation` MEANS `the s 11 product` `the car's cost price` `the rate` `days owned in that first FBT year` (`the number of days in the year of tax` `the FBT year it was bought in`)
        `the value after the first year` MEANS `the car's cost price` MINUS `the first year's depreciation`

§§ `s 136(1) -- business use percentage`

-- s 136(1) "business use percentage", from the authorised rendering:
--     (Number of business kilometres travelled by the car during the holding period / Total number of kilometres travelled by the
--      car during the holding period) × 100%
@export What is the business use percentage of my car for the year (s 136(1))?
GIVEN `business kilometres` IS A NUMBER @desc The kilometres the car travelled on business journeys in the holding period (the employer's estimate from the log book and odometer records)
      `total kilometres` IS A NUMBER @desc The total kilometres the car travelled in the holding period
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The business use percentage of my car` MEANS
    (`business kilometres` TIMES 100) DIVIDED BY `total kilometres`

§§ `s 10 -- taxable value of my car under the cost basis`

-- s 10(2), from the authorised rendering:   (C × (100% − BP)) − R
-- "C is the operating cost of the car during the holding period; BP is: (a) if, under section 10A or 10B, the employer is not
-- entitled to a reduction in the operating cost of the car on account of business journeys ... -- nil; or (c) in any other case
-- -- the business use percentage applicable to the car for the holding period; and R is the amount (if any) of the recipient's
-- payment."
-- s 10(3)(a): the operating cost is the car expenses (other than insured repairs, registration and insurance) "incurred during
-- the holding period"; the registration and insurance attributable to it; for an owned car, the depreciation and interest deemed
-- under s 11 for the holding period; for a leased car, the lease charges attributable to it. As for s 9 (NOTES.md finding 4), a
-- recipient's payment above C x (100% - BP) is read as bringing the value to nil, not below.
DECLARE `How the provider holds the car` IS ONE OF
    `owned`
    `leased`

GIVEN `operating cost` IS A NUMBER, `business use percentage` IS A NUMBER, `recipient's payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cost basis value` MEANS
    IF `the private part` GREATER THAN `recipient's payment` THEN `the private part` MINUS `recipient's payment` ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the private part` MEANS (`operating cost` TIMES (100 MINUS `business use percentage`)) DIVIDED BY 100

@export What is the operating cost of my employer's car for the FBT year (ss 10(3)(a), 11)?
GIVEN `how the car is held` IS A `How the provider holds the car` @desc Whether your employer (or the provider) owns or leases the car
      `car expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Fuel, oil, servicing, repairs and tyres for the year, by anyone, leaving out repairs paid for by insurance or compensation, in dollars
      `registration and insurance` IS A NUMBER @desc The registration and insurance attributable to the year, in dollars
      `lease charges` IS A NUMBER @desc For a leased car, the lease charges attributable to the year; 0 for an owned car
      `value for depreciation and interest` IS A NUMBER @desc For an owned car, its depreciated value at the start of the FBT year (or its cost price if bought during the year); 0 for a leased car
      `days owned in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc For an owned car, the days in the FBT year it was owned (taken as the days it was held)
      `the FBT year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the FBT year starts
      `DV percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 diminishing value percentage (200 for a car held from 10 May 2006)
      `effective life in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The car's effective life in the Commissioner's determination (8 years for most cars)
      `the statutory interest rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The statutory (benchmark) interest rate for the FBT year, as a percentage
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The operating cost of the car` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the car is held`
    WHEN `leased` THEN `car expenses` PLUS `registration and insurance` PLUS `lease charges`
    WHEN `owned` THEN `car expenses` PLUS `registration and insurance` PLUS `the depreciation` PLUS `the interest`
    WHERE
        `D` MEANS `the number of days in the year of tax` `the FBT year starting in`
        `the depreciation` MEANS `the holding period share` (`the s 11 product` `value for depreciation and interest` (`the depreciation rate B` `DV percentage` `effective life in years`) `days owned in the year` `D`) `days owned in the year` `days owned in the year`
        `the interest` MEANS `the holding period share` (`the s 11 product` `value for depreciation and interest` (`the statutory interest rate` DIVIDED BY 100) `days owned in the year` `D`) `days owned in the year` `days owned in the year`

@export What is the taxable value of my car under the cost basis, before the s 10(5) comparison (s 10(2))?
GIVEN `operating cost` IS A NUMBER @desc The operating cost of the car for the holding period (see the operating cost question), in dollars
      `log book and odometer records kept` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ss 10A or 10B entitle your employer to reduce the operating cost for business journeys (the log book and odometer records were kept and the business use percentage specified)
      `business use percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The business use percentage for the holding period
      `what I paid towards the car` IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid towards the car during the year and were not reimbursed (fuel and other car expenses only with the declaration or documents in time), in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The cost basis taxable value of my car` MEANS
    `the cost basis value` `operating cost` (IF `log book and odometer records kept` THEN `business use percentage` ELSE 0) `what I paid towards the car`

-- s 10(5): where the employer elects the cost basis and the value under s 10(2) "exceeds the taxable value ... that would have
-- been ascertained under section 9 if that election had not been made", the Act applies "as if that election had not been made".
-- So the taxable value is the lower of the two. The statutory formula value is fbtaa-employee.l4's `The taxable value of my car`.
@export What is the taxable value of my car if my employer elected the cost basis (s 10(1), (2), (5))?
GIVEN `operating cost` IS A NUMBER @desc The operating cost of the car for the holding period, in dollars
      `log book and odometer records kept` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ss 10A or 10B entitle your employer to reduce the operating cost for business journeys
      `business use percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The business use percentage for the holding period
      `what I paid towards the car` IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid towards the car during the year and were not reimbursed, in dollars
      `the car's cost price` IS A NUMBER @desc For the statutory formula: the cost price of the car to your employer when first held (or its leased car value then)
      `the day my employer first held the car` IS A DATE @desc For the statutory formula: the earliest day your employer (or its associate) held the car
      `the FBT year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the FBT year starts
      `the cost of non-business accessories added` IS A NUMBER @desc For the statutory formula: non-business accessories fitted later and still fitted; 0 if none
      `the days the car was available to me` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in the FBT year on which the car was provided to you
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The taxable value of my car under the cost basis election` MEANS
    IF `the cost basis` GREATER THAN `the statutory formula` THEN `the statutory formula` ELSE `the cost basis`
    WHERE
        `the cost basis` MEANS `The cost basis taxable value of my car` `operating cost` `log book and odometer records kept` `business use percentage` `what I paid towards the car`
        `the statutory formula` MEANS `The taxable value of my car` `the car's cost price` `the day my employer first held the car` `the FBT year starting in` `the cost of non-business accessories added` `the days the car was available to me` `what I paid towards the car`

§§ `Mirror questions -- the same rules, from the employer's side`

@export As the employer, what reportable fringe benefits amount must I report for this employee, as a s 57A or s 58 employer or otherwise (ss 135P, 135Q)?
GIVEN `the employee's individual fringe benefits amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The total taxable value of the non-exempt fringe benefits you provided to this employee in the FBT year, leaving out excluded fringe benefits
      `the employee's individual quasi-fringe benefits amount` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are a s 57A or s 58 employer, the total taxable value your exempt benefits to this employee would have if they were fringe benefits; 0 otherwise
      `the FBT year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the FBT year started
      `I am a charity, hospital, ambulance service or other s 57A or s 58 employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a public benevolent institution, health promotion charity, public or non-profit hospital, public ambulance service, or an employer of the kind in s 58
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`As the employer, the reportable amount, any employer` MEANS
    `My reportable fringe benefits amount, any employer` `the employee's individual fringe benefits amount` `the employee's individual quasi-fringe benefits amount` `the FBT year starting in` `I am a charity, hospital, ambulance service or other s 57A or s 58 employer`

@export As the employer, what is the taxable value of the car I provide to this employee, where I elected the cost basis (s 10)?
GIVEN `operating cost` IS A NUMBER @desc The operating cost of the car for the holding period, in dollars
      `log book and odometer records kept` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ss 10A or 10B entitle you to reduce the operating cost for business journeys
      `business use percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The business use percentage for the holding period
      `what the employee paid towards the car` IS A NUMBER @desc What the employee paid towards the car during the year and you did not reimburse, in dollars
      `the car's cost price` IS A NUMBER @desc For the statutory formula: the cost price of the car to you when first held (or its leased car value then)
      `the day I first held the car` IS A DATE @desc For the statutory formula: the earliest day you (or your associate) held the car
      `the FBT year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the FBT year starts
      `the cost of non-business accessories added` IS A NUMBER @desc For the statutory formula: non-business accessories fitted later and still fitted; 0 if none
      `the days the car was available to the employee` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in the FBT year on which the car was provided to the employee
GIVETH A NUMBER
`As the employer, the taxable value of the car under the cost basis` MEANS
    `The taxable value of my car under the cost basis election` `operating cost` `log book and odometer records kept` `business use percentage` `what the employee paid towards the car` `the car's cost price` `the day I first held the car` `the FBT year starting in` `the cost of non-business accessories added` `the days the car was available to the employee`
